00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:08.740
and style vectors. Hydrahead fuses full and linear attention at head granularity rather than

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:16.080
layer granularity. It preserves full attention only on retrieval critical heads. After a three-stage

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:23.180
transfer pipeline, it matches a 3 to 1 layer wise hybrid's long context performance at a 7 to 1

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:32.260
L A to F A ratio while training on only 15 B tokens. The approach yields more than 69% improvement

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:40.200
over baseline at 512 K context. Long context model builders should study the interpretability driven

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:45.680
head selection method. Okay, let's pop the hood on head level attention hybridization.

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:52.180
Everyone talks about hybrid attention as a simple layer wise swap between full and linear attention.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:58.460
In practice, the decision is finer green because heads inside the same layer already specialize.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:05.760
Some focus on retrieval while others handle local patterns. Hydrahead therefore keeps full attention

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:12.280
only on the retrieval critical heads identified through interpretability analysis. It routes the

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:18.800
rest through linear attention. Orthogonalization prevents the distributional shift that would otherwise

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:25.520
accumulate when mixing the two output distributions. The resulting model reaches 69% gains

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:33.460
at 512 K context after training on just 15 B tokens. This shows that head level selection

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:40.020
recovers most of the quality of denser hybrids at far lower cost. When your workload is retrieval

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:47.280
heavy and context exceeds 128 K, start with head level hybridization rather than uniform layer

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:53.460
replacement. The main gacha is that head selection must be redone when the base model or domain

00:09:53.460 --> 00:10:00.360
changes. This development moves the open weight models arc forward by narrowing the gap with closed

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:06.780
frontier systems on long context retrieval without proportional increases in training tokens.

